<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Arabic. Also the library's right-to-left reference locale: the phone field puts a dial code and
  Latin digits inside an RTL paragraph, which is the layout most likely to break, so previews and
  UI tests exercise this locale specifically.

  Arabic takes all six CLDR plural categories (zero/one/two/few/many/other); leaving any of them out
  makes the platform fall back to "other" and read wrongly for 2, 3-10 and 11-99.
-->
